{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18570 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Ancistrolikokine C is implicated in the target pathway leading to Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple intermediate proteins. The evidence suggests that Ancistrolikokine C directly targets Protein delta homolog 1, which in turn is a target of various compounds, including Iso-3-Thujyl Acetate and Olean-12-ene-3beta,22alpha,28-triol. These intermediates all ultimately have Phosphodiesterase 6C as their target. The consistent presence of these intermediates in the pathway, coupled with the high confidence scores in the relationships, indicates a well-defined mechanism where Ancistrolikokine C acts as a central node in a network that ultimately leads to the inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Ancistrolikokine C in modulating the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction between Ancistrolikokine C and the intermediate proteins remains to be fully elucidated.",
